{"ts":"2026-11-23T16:50:45.011823878Z","author":"investigation-dev","event":"ReviewerVoted","data":{"review_id":"cr-2e0p1w","vote":"lgtm","reason":"LGTM from the lead. Opt-in and additive: the default and partial/interrupted semantics are unchanged, and strict mode is refused unless completion is complete. The mismatch is checked in plan() before the seal, so the handle stays open, and the missing/unexpected arrays come from BTreeSet differences, so they are sorted. The tests cover atomic refusal, correction with the same key, lost-response replay, key reuse and replay after retirement. Non-blocking nit: in strict mode, a declared key that names an appended fact is now reported under 'missing' rather than with the clearer fact-key message. It is documented ('appended facts are outside the artifact inventory'), so keep it if that was intended. The workspace is stale against main (W12/W14/PERF merges); sync before merging. I will merge it through edict once the bone is done.","target_commit":"8a4be490f8e5db557e1615b3314bb5d9547e9db2"}}
